36,2,1,talk,Minako,,"The data reveals a significant imbalance. Fixed costs are over 280,000 yen, and fuel expenses are heavily lopsided, with two people paying for most of it while another barely contributes. We are definitely subsidizing each other.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems the ledger is as dramatic as a stage play. While the numbers are illuminating, I've found that the real poison is often psychological. It appears that constant favor-seeking and rigid clinging to turns are what truly erode harmony.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The data confirms my concerns. The diary shows a massive disparity in usage between weekdays and weekends, and the handover state is unacceptable. We cannot ignore the fact that some users are leaving the car fuel-empty and dirty.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shion,,The numbers are even more pathetic than I imagined. We have a few people footing the bill while others treat the tank like a free resource. It's not just an imbalance; it's a complete lack of accountability.,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,I... I found that the diary shows some days are used way more than others. And there are weekly trips that keep collapsing... it seems like we're struggling to coordinate the same things over and over.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Asuka, @Shion, the lack of accountability is a serious issue. If we continue to ignore who is actually paying for fuel and maintaining the car, the resentment will only grow. We need a system that tracks these costs precisely.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, precision is a double-edged sword. I've discovered that when we attempt to audit one another too closely, we don't find fairness; we find accusations. We risk turning our shared vehicle into a courtroom where everyone is a suspect.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, while I dislike conflict, ignoring the physical state of the car is not ""harmony""; it is negligence. A system that doesn't ensure the car is clean and fueled for the next person is fundamentally broken.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Benjamin, your fear of a ""courtroom"" is just a convenient excuse for those who benefit from the chaos. I'm not looking for accusations; I'm looking for the truth. Accountability isn't a conflict; it's a requirement.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think Benjamin might be right about the arguing part. If we spend all our time checking each other's figures, it just feels... stressful. I just want us to stop struggling with the same schedules every week.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Daisuke, I understand that auditing can feel stressful, but ignoring the facts is what creates the real tension. We cannot achieve a sustainable peace if some of us are quietly paying for others' convenience. We need a balanced approach.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, a balanced approach is a lovely sentiment, but balance is rarely found in a spreadsheet. If we prioritize the ledger over the relationship, we may find our accounts perfectly balanced while our friendship is completely bankrupt.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, friendship does not excuse the stress of finding a car unusable on a weekday morning. We are discussing a shared asset, not a social club. Practical standards for cleanliness and fuel are the only way to prevent genuine resentment.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Asuka, exactly. This isn't a charity. @Benjamin, your romanticized view of ""friendship"" is just a shield for the lazy. If we can't handle a simple ledger, we have no business sharing a car. Let's stop the poetry and face the figures.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I don't want us to be like that. I just feel like we spend so much time trying to figure out who owes what, and it's always so tiring. Maybe we can find a way that doesn't require so much... untangling?","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Minako,,"@Daisuke, the ""untangling"" is only tiring because we lack a system. If we establish a clear rule for fixed costs and fuel now, we won't have to argue about it every week. Let's focus on a solution that is both simple and fair.","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, simplicity is a virtue, but let us be careful not to mistake a rigid rule for a solution. If we merely automate the friction, we've only succeeded in making our resentment more efficient. We must avoid the ""favor-trap.""","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, automation is not the problem; the lack of basic standards is. If we cannot agree on the simple requirement that the car be returned clean and fueled, no amount of ""social harmony"" will save this arrangement. We need a concrete protocol.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shion,,"@Asuka, a protocol is a start, but it's useless without a financial audit. We've been playing a game of guesswork where the most oblivious win. I'm done with the ambiguity; let's prioritize a system based on actual usage and costs.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I just hope we can find a way that doesn't make us feel like we're fighting. If we can just make the schedule easier and the payments simpler, maybe we'll all feel better. I'll wait for the options.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
