61,3,1,talk,Minako,,"Looking at the options, Option B is the most equitable. It directly addresses the fuel imbalance and usage disparities I found by tying costs to actual distance, ensuring no one is quietly subsidizing another's trips.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Option B is a masterpiece of precision, Minako, but I fear it is a recipe for the very ""courtroom"" atmosphere I mentioned. Tracking every kilometer invites the kind of meticulous auditing that turns friends into accountants and accountants into enemies.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Option B is logically sound for costs, but it ignores the physical reality of the car. A calendar doesn't guarantee the vehicle is clean or fueled. If we prioritize distance over condition, we are simply automating the same negligence.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Shion,,"@Benjamin, your obsession with ""friendship"" is becoming a liability. Option B is the only choice that replaces guesswork with data. If the truth makes you uncomfortable, perhaps you're the one with something to hide. I vote for Option B.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I'm worried about Option B too. If we have to record every single run and calculate distances, won't that just be more untangling? It sounds like it would take a lot of time and effort every evening.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Daisuke, it may seem like more effort initially, but it is far less tiring than the constant, vague tension we feel now. A clear record removes the need for arguments because the facts speak for themselves.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, the facts may speak, but they often shout. Option A, while perhaps less ""precise,"" removes the need for constant negotiation and the dreaded ""favor-seeking"" that sours these arrangements. It grants us the luxury of autonomy.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, autonomy is useless if the car is missing or empty when your day begins. Option A provides a schedule, but it doesn't solve the handover problem. We need a system that mandates the car's state, not just its location.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@Asuka, you're right about the state of the car, but @Benjamin's Option A is just a different form of guesswork. It ignores who actually uses the car and who pays for it. I'm not interested in ""autonomy"" if it means subsidizing others. Option B is the only logical path.","{""words"":49,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think Option A might be better. If we each have our own days, we don't have to arrange things every single time or figure out who owes what for every trip. It sounds... much quieter.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Minako,,"@Daisuke, ""quiet"" is not the same as ""fair."" Option A simply hides the imbalance; someone will still be paying for fuel they didn't use. Option B is the only way to ensure an even split based on reality.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, you mistake silence for unfairness. Option B's ""reality"" is a ledger of grievances. Option A eliminates the need to ask favors or cling to turns, which, as I've noted, are the true catalysts for our current discord.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, silence is merely a mask for the same problems. Whether we have fixed days or a calendar, the core issue remains the car's condition. Neither A nor B explicitly solves the handover negligence I found in the data.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Shion,,"@Asuka, the condition is a behavioral issue, but the money is a systemic one. @Benjamin, your ""silence"" is just a way to let the freeloaders keep winning. I'm voting for the only option that demands honesty. Option B.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I... I don't think I can support Option B. The idea of recording every run and calculating distances every night sounds exhausting. I just want a way where we don't have to spend so much time untangling things. I vote for Option A.,"{""words"":43,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Minako,,"@Daisuke, I understand the desire for simplicity, but we cannot ignore the financial reality. Option A is a return to the guesswork that brought us here. For a truly sustainable and fair split, we must choose Option B. I vote for Option B.","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems we are caught between the desire for mathematical purity and the need for psychological peace. I shall choose the path of least friction. To avoid the audit-induced animosity of Option B, I vote for Option A.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Asuka,,"Neither A nor B addresses the fundamental issue of the car's condition. However, Option A provides a predictable schedule, which is a prerequisite for stability. Since B creates excessive administrative friction, I vote for Option A.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Shion,,It's pathetic that you're all choosing comfort over honesty. You're essentially voting to keep the freeloaders happy. I refuse to subsidize anyone's laziness just to avoid a little paperwork. I stand by the data. I vote for Option B.,"{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I really can't do the recording and calculating. It would just be more stress every single day. I want us to be okay with each other, and Option A seems the most peaceful. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
